1352	=== README.md
1353	     1	# GIF Editor
1354	     2	
1355	     3	A client-side GIF editor that runs entirely in the browser. No uploads, no servers — your files never leave your machine.
1356	     4	
1357	     5	**Live:** [https://abhisingh.in/gif-editor/](https://abhisingh.in/gif-editor/)
1358	     6	
1359	     7	## Features
1360	     8	
1361	     9	- **Resize** — scale with aspect ratio lock and quick presets (25%, 50%, 75%, 200%)
1362	    10	- **Crop** — interactive drag-to-draw, move, and corner-resize crop area with ratio presets (1:1, 4:3, 16:9)
1363	    11	- **Compress** — reduce colors (8–256) and FPS with two-pass palette optimization
1364	    12	- **Speed** — adjust playback speed from 0.25× to 4×
1365	    13	- **Trim** — cut start/end by time
1366	    14	- **Reverse** — reverse frame order
1367	    15	- **Frame Editing** — extract frames, delete or drag-to-reorder, reassemble at custom FPS
1368	    16	- **Filters** — brightness, contrast, saturation, grayscale with presets
1369	    17	- **Slack Emoji Export** — one-click preset that center-crops to square and iteratively compresses to ≤128 KB
1370	    18	- **Batch Slack Export** — drop several GIFs at once and download them all Slack-ready in one `.zip`, with original filenames kept
1371	    19	
1372	    20	## Tech Stack
1373	    21	
1374	    22	- **Vanilla JS** (ES modules) — no framework
1375	    23	- **Tailwind CSS v4** — via `@tailwindcss/vite` plugin
1376	    24	- **FFmpeg.wasm** — WebAssembly build of FFmpeg for all GIF processing
1377	    25	- **Vite** — dev server and bundler
1378	    26	
1379	    27	## Browser Support
1380	    28	
1381	    29	Chrome, Edge, and Firefox. Safari is not supported (SharedArrayBuffer restrictions).
1382	    30	
1383	    31	## Getting Started
1384	    32	
1385	    33	```bash
1386	    34	npm install
1387	    35	npm run dev
1388	    36	```
1389	    37	
1390	    38	Opens at `http://localhost:5173` with required COOP/COEP headers.
1391	    39	
1392	    40	### Production Build
1393	    41	
1394	    42	```bash
1395	    43	npm run build
1396	    44	npm run preview
1397	    45	```
1398	    46	
1399	    47	## How It Works
1400	    48	
1401	    49	All processing happens client-side via FFmpeg.wasm:
1402	    50	
1403	    51	1. **Lazy loading** — FFmpeg.wasm (~25 MB) loads on first GIF drop, with a progress bar
1404	    52	2. **IndexedDB caching** — WASM binary is cached after first download for instant reloads
1405	    53	3. **Two-pass palette** — compress and Slack export use palettegen → paletteuse for quality
1406	    54	4. **Operation replay undo** — stores operation history instead of full blobs, replays from original on undo
1407	    55	
1408	    56	## Deployment
1409	    57	
1410	    58	Deployed to GitHub Pages via Actions. The `coi-serviceworker` injects `Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy` and `Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy` headers required by FFmpeg.wasm on static hosts.
1411	    59	
1412	    60	## License
1413	    61	
1414	    62	MIT — see [LICENSE](LICENSE).
1415	    63	
1416	    64	---
